            <ArticleTitle>Drug abuse during the Civil War (1861-1865).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1007-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Civil War (1861-1865) has long been blamed as the catalyst for the spread of drug addiction in America. This paper attempts to examine this hypothesis through an extensive review of pertinent literature, and to clarify misconceptions concerning addiction problems associated with the war.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
